README: PODFoam snapshot fix and validation

The four solvers this series touches build on v2012, v2106, v2212 and 8.
The README says so without widening the version list of the other
examples. A pointer under PODFoam in Contents names the validation, what
a module must provide and the versions it passes on. The prep_env.sh
sentence says that its source line must point at the bashrc of the
OpenFOAM version in use. The requirements are given per solver: the
solvers need Python 3 with numpy and the headers, and a list gives what
each shipped module imports beyond that.

